\varphi_t(x) &= \log \mu_t(x) - \log \int_{\mathcal{X}} \pi'(x,y) e^{\psi_t(y)} dy, \\
\psi_t(y) &= \log \nu_t(y) - \log \int_{\mathcal{X}} \pi'(x,y) e^{\varphi_t(x)} dx.
\end{aligned}
\end{equation}

By Lemma \ref{lem:density_bounds}, $\log \mu_t$ and $\log \nu_t$ are uniformly bounded. By Assumption \ref{ass:coupling_regularity}, the effective kernel $-\log \pi'$ is bounded. Viewing \eqref{eq:phipsi_sinkhorn} as standard EOT dual equations, these bounds directly guarantee uniform $L^\infty$ bounds for $\varphi_t$ and $\psi_t$ (e.g., Lemma 4.9 in \cite{nutz2021introduction}), establishing $C_{\infty}$.

For spatial regularity, differencing \eqref{eq:phipsi_sinkhorn} for any $x_1, x_2 \in \mathcal{X}$ gives:
